<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine monthly oilseed crushings.</title>
<headline>Argentine monthly oilseed crushings.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine mills crushed 1,523,763 tonnes of oilseed in December 1996 against 1,142,235 tonnes in December 1995, the Agriculture Secretariat said. (Breakdown in tonnes, year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> Soybean		 733,107    (855,772)</p>
<p> Sunflowerseed	 259,733    (268,544)</p>
<p> Linseed		   1,540     (10,128)</p>
<p> Groundnutseed	  13,446	(7,791)</p>
<p> Cottonseed		  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p>Output in December was as follows:</p>
<p> ..............Oils...................Meals</p>
<p> Soybean     129,857    (155,940)    585,202     (705,596)</p>
<p> Sunflower   107,115    (108,765)    112,458     (111,266)</p>
<p> Linseed	   492	(3,043)	  nil	   (nil)</p>
<p> Groundnut     5,224	(2,853)	7,739	 (4,496)</p>
<p> Cottonseed	nil	  (nil)	  nil	   (nil)</p>
<p> .......................Expellers</p>
<p> Soybean    2,373   (2,960)  Groundnut   nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Sunflower    nil     (nil)  Cottonseed  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Linseed    1,027   (6,441)</p>
<p>Crushings from January to December, with the same period in 1995 in brackets, were:</p>
<p> Soybean	    10,359,937    (9,103,046)</p>
<p> Sunflowerseed     5,043,314    (4,944,786)</p>
<p> Linseed		 129,891	(142,024)</p>
<p> Groundnutseed	 157,035	(126,587)</p>
<p> Cottonseed	    432,947	(419,616)</p>
<p>Output in January through December (1995 in brackets):</p>
<p> ..............Oils...................Meals</p>
<p> Soybean   1,838,339  (1,599,486)  8,281,810  (7,331,042)</p>
<p> Sunflower 2,034,022, (1,974,800)  2,124,614  (2,097,786)</p>
<p> Linseed	39,415     (46,986)	  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Groundnut    60,719     (48,844)     90,253     (71,503)</p>
<p> Cottonseed   66m659     (64,902)    205,507    (194,791)</p>
<p> .......................Expellers</p>
<p> Soybean    34,665 (52,956)   Groundnut   nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Sunflower   6,419  (4,234)   Cottonseed  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Linseed    80,419 (81,446)</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
